## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to model simple domain data, perform file-based persistence with Codable, and drive UI with SwiftUI while handling dates and basic filtering.

## Key Concepts
- SwiftUI List and navigation
- Codable JSON persistence to Documents
- File I/O and error handling
- Date arithmetic for overdue
- Lightweight test scaffolding

## Code Example
```swift
struct Task: Codable {
  let id: UUID
  var title: String
  var dueDate: Date
  var isDone: Bool
}

final class TaskStore {
  private var tasks: [Task] = []
  private let url: URL
  init(filename: String = "tasks.json") {
    let dir = FileManager.default.urls(for: .documentDirectory, in: .userDomainMask).first!
    self.url = dir.appendingPathComponent(filename)
    load()
  }
  func load() {
    if let data = try? Data(contentsOf: url), let decoded = try? JSONDecoder().decode([Task].self, from: data) {
      tasks = decoded
    }
  }
  func save() {
    if let data = try? JSONEncoder().encode(tasks) {
      try? data.write(to: url)
    }
  }
  // add/edit/delete helpers...
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you migrate to Core Data if the feature set grows? 
- How would you detect and recover from partial write failures?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design an offline-first image pipeline with robust caching, memory management, and accessibility in a real UI scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Two-tier caching (memory + disk)
- LRU eviction under memory pressure
- Prefetching and cancellation tied to visible cells
- Accessibility: Dynamic Type and VoiceOver labels
- Async/await data loading and main-thread UI updates

## Code Example
```swift
import UIKit

actor ImageLoader {
    private let memCache = NSCache<NSString, UIImage>()
    private let fileManager = FileManager.default
    private let diskDir: URL

    init(diskFolder: URL) { self.diskDir = diskFolder }

    func load(from url: URL) async -> UIImage? {
        let key = url.absoluteString as NSString
        if let image = memCache.object(forKey: key) { return image }
        let path = diskDir.appendingPathComponent(url.lastPathComponent)
        if let data = try? Data(contentsOf: path), let image = UIImage(data: data) {
            memCache.setObject(image, forKey: key)
            return image
        }
        guard let (data, _) = try? await URLSession.shared.data(from: url),
              let image = UIImage(data: data) else { return nil }
        memCache.setObject(image, forKey: key)
        try? data.write(to: path)
        return image
    }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This probes Swift Concurrency mastery (actors, TaskGroups), deterministic UI ordering, and robust back-end latency handling in a data-labeling workflow.

## Key Concepts
- Swift Concurrency: actors, TaskGroup
- AsyncSequence and backpressure
- MainActor UI updates
- Local persistence (SQLite/GRDB)
- Exponential backoff and cancellation

